# Ignore rules for the apex (Level 1) JavaScript tier.
#
# `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` must print nothing after a full
# check, test, serve and container cycle. That emptiness is an asserted gate, not
# a nicety. No ignore rules existed here before the /health endpoint was added
# because nothing in this repository had ever been executed -- there was no
# residue to ignore. Running `node --test` with a coverage reporter, running an
# npm script, or redirecting server output changes that, and every pattern below
# exists because one of those produces the file it names.
#
# Scope is this repository only. `child_repo_10_LOC` is a submodule -- a separate
# Git repository with its own index and its own ignore rules -- so these patterns
# neither reach into it nor need to. Python residue (`__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`)
# belongs to Level 2's own file and Java residue (`*.class`) to Level 3's; nothing
# below is borrowed from another language, because this tier cannot produce it.
#
# Every pattern here is deliberately narrow. The tracked payload at this tier is
# small and all of it is load-bearing, so a broad pattern is expensive. `*.json`
# would silence package.json and config/health.json -- health.js reads both and
# falls back to compiled-in literals rather than failing, so losing them would
# leave the endpoint answering 200 with an identity this repository never
# declared, a failure with no symptom. `config/` and `docs/` would silence the
# serving configuration and the normative contract, `*.yml` the workflow, `test*`
# and `*.test.js` the contract test suite, and a bare `.env*` the tracked
# .env.example template. None of those appears below, and any future edit should
# be checked with `git check-ignore -v <path>` rather than by reading.

# Installed dependency tree, plus the npm cache when it is redirected into the
# repository with `npm --cache .npm`. This tier has no dependencies at all --
# every module it loads is a Node built-in -- so these two lines are defensive:
# an accidental `npm install` must never become a committable directory.
node_modules/
.npm/

# Local environment file. It is the one untracked file in this workflow: it holds
# real values for the two variables .env.example documents, and a real value does
# not belong in history.
#
# The names are spelled out one at a time instead of using `.env*` precisely so
# that .env.example -- a tracked, reviewed template carrying no real value --
# stays visible to Git. No negation such as `!.env.example` is needed, and none is
# used, because no pattern here matches that name in the first place.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Run and log residue. `npm-debug.log` appears when an npm script fails, and a
# plain `*.log` covers redirected server output such as
# `node server.js > server.log 2>&1`, which is how this endpoint is started in the
# background both locally and in continuous integration. `logs/` covers the same
# output collected into a directory. No tracked file at this tier ends in `.log`.
npm-debug.log*
*.log
logs/

# Coverage output. `node --test --experimental-test-coverage` with the lcov
# reporter writes `lcov.info` beside package.json, and `NODE_V8_COVERAGE=coverage`
# writes a directory of raw V8 profiles. Both are per-run artefacts produced *by*
# index.test.js and are never input *to* it -- the suite itself writes only under
# the system temporary directory, so it leaves nothing else here.
coverage/
lcov.info
*.lcov

# Operating-system and editor scratch files. Short on purpose: these are the ones
# that actually turn up, from a file manager or an interrupted `vi` session, and
# they are never content.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Deliberately NOT ignored, each for a reason worth stating once:
#
#   child_repo_10_LOC   The submodule gitlink. It is first-class project source
#                       rather than a vendored artefact -- it receives this same
#                       feature at its own tier -- so no pattern here may match
#                       its name, and none does.
#   .gitmodules         Its declaration; tracked, and unchanged by this feature.
#   package.json        Identity: the `name` and `version` the payload reports.
#   config/health.json  Serving configuration: host, port, path, status literal.
#   .env.example        The tracked template documenting PORT and HOST.
#   .nvmrc              The Node version pin, single-sourced for CI and readers.
#   index.js            The application, whose five-line legacy output a
#                       regression gate fingerprints byte for byte.
#   health.js           The payload builder and request handler, and the
#   server.js           long-lived entry point that binds the listener.
#   index.test.js       The contract test suite.
#   Dockerfile          The container definition, and the build-context denylist
#   .dockerignore       that excludes *this* file from an image -- the mirror
#                       image of what this file does for Git.
#   README.md docs/     Documentation, including the normative contract document.
#   .github/workflows/  The workflow that asserts the gate described at the top.
